.TH SSHTEST 1
.SH NAME
sshtest \- test the ssh(2) transport against a real sshd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshtest
[
.I host
]
.br
.B sshtest exec
.I addr user keyfile wantthumb cmd expectout
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sshtest
exercises the
.IR ssh (2)
transport end to end against a live SSH server \(em
.B github.com:22
by default \(em and proves three things:
.IP \(bu
the
.B curve25519-sha256
key exchange and the
.B rsa-sha2-256
host-key signature verify:
.B connect
only returns if the server's signature over the exchange hash checks
out;
.IP \(bu
the host-key thumbprint computed matches GitHub's published RSA
fingerprint, an independent oracle (\c
.B ssh-keyscan -t rsa github.com
.B "| ssh-keygen -lf -"
on a Unix host yields the same
.B SHA256:
value);
.B connect
is asked to fail closed unless it matches;
.IP \(bu
the
.B chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com
packet cipher round-trips: after
.B NEWKEYS
an
.I encrypted
.B SERVICE_REQUEST
is sent and a validly-tagged
.B SERVICE_ACCEPT
must come back. That single exchange is what validates the key
derivation, the two-key length/payload split, the per-packet IV, the
block-aligned payload and the padding rule together \(em none of which
the plaintext key exchange touches.
.PP
As an automated negative control, a second
.B connect
is then made with a deliberately wrong expected thumbprint and must be
refused; a refused connection is a safe computation, so unlike most
controls in this tree it need not be run by hand.
.PP
The host name is resolved through this tree's own DoH resolver (\c
.IR doh (2)),
since dial-by-name is not available under hosted
.IR emu .
With a
.I host
argument the oracle checks are skipped (only that host has a baked-in
fingerprint), but the key exchange, signature verification and
encrypted round trip still run.
.PP
The
.B exec
form drives the full client \(em transport, publickey
authentication and command execution \(em against a server at
.I addr
(a dial string), authenticating as
.I user
with the PEM RSA key in
.IR keyfile ,
pinning the host thumbprint to
.I wantthumb
(fail-closed), running
.I cmd
and asserting its exit status is zero and its standard output equals
.IR expectout .
It is meant to be run against a hermetic local
.IR sshd :
.I /tests/sshlocal.sh
sets one up with a generated host key and one authorised key, runs
.B "sshtest exec"
against it (with the thumbprint oracle
from
.IR ssh-keygen ),
and adds a negative control \(em a second run with an
.I unauthorised
key that must be rejected.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/sshtest.b
.br
.B /tests/sshlocal.sh
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ssh (2),
.IR chachatest (1),
.IR doh (2)
.SH BUGS
The default form requires a working network path to the server on port
22, and the thumbprint oracle is checked only for the default
.BR github.com .
The
.B exec
form requires a host
.I sshd
and
.IR ssh-keygen ;
.I /tests/sshlocal.sh
skips (exit 2) when they are absent.
